[_] Allow a lone open-bracket inside description notes $CANCELLED 2026-08-05 after design review. A lone opening bracket remains reserved because it may begin a double-bracket link. Literal opening brackets in descriptions must be escaped as \[; unescaped use is a precise parser-integrity error. This avoids a lexical-precedence hierarchy between links, action states, and prose.$ !2 %2026-08-05T21:22 #019f76e0-ea98-7e73-9301-d7f1d7945722
[x] Restore canonical grammar corpus tests $DONE 2026-08-05. Grammar tests now generate ignored corpus files from checked-in examples and reviewed expected trees before tree-sitter test. Negative parse examples are supported; 28 canonical cases actually execute. Bracket escaping, unescaped-bracket failure, and incomplete-link recovery live in the standard corpus; the Node binding test is load-only.$ !2 %2026-08-05T21:46 #019fd565-201c-7932-8a05-8ede31a25d97
